1]Explain indetail about Aggregation and Composition ?

	->In java thier are 2types of relationships:-
		i)is-a relationship
		ii)has-a relationship
	->is-a relationship can be achieved by making use of inheritance
	->has-a relationship can be achieved by making use of aggregation and composition
	->has-relationship is of 2 types:-
		i)loosely coupled has-a relationship
		ii)tightly couples has-a relationship
		
	->In loosely coupled has-a relationship the aggregate object exists
	->In tightly coupled has-a relationship the composite object exists
	
Aggregate Objects:-
===================
	->Aggregate objects are such objects which can be accessed even though enclosing object is not accessible

Composite Objects:-
===================
	->Composite objects are such objects which are not accessible if the enclosing object is not accessible.



2]Explain indetail about serialization and de-serialization ?

	->Serialization is the mechanism of converting the state of an object into byte stream is called as
	serialization
	->Where as de-serialization is the reverse process,where the byte stream is used to re-create the actual
	java object in memory is called as de-serialization
	->If i dont want to serialize any data then i use trasient keyword
	->After serializing the data,if i change the serial version UID then de-serialization will not work
	because the serial version UID is changed,so serial version UID should be same while doing serialization
	and de-serialization
